L9-A: env-gated guest-function-entry trace for the instrumented-Xenia golden oracle.

Adds a per-guest-function-entry trace emit, gated by XENIA_GUEST_TRACE=1, that
writes fixed-width (guest_pc, lr, r3, r1, thread_id, tag) records to a binary
file (default xenia_boot.trace). This is the L9-A "golden oracle": a ground-truth
ordered trace of a working boot to the Superman Returns menu, consumed by the
L9-C divergence bisector.

The hook lives in GuestFunction::Call (src/xenia/cpu/function.cc), which is the
backend-agnostic C++ choke point every guest-function entry that re-enters the
guest from host/kernel code flows through. See tools/xenia-trace/README.md for
the COVERAGE CAVEAT (guest->guest JIT-internal bl calls bypass this site) and the
documented JIT-prolog upgrade path for a complete per-function trace.

The on-disk record format is defined in the added header src/xenia/cpu/xenia_trace.h.

Verified against xenia-canary @ 0b4e6c440e91f118b42a5e9e32a6b629ce4c387c
(2026-06-24). `git apply --check` passes against that revision.

TO APPLY (from the xenia-canary repo root):
    cp ../../tools/xenia-trace/xenia_trace.h src/xenia/cpu/xenia_trace.h
    git apply ../../tools/xenia-trace/xenia_trace.patch

(The header is copied in as a plain file rather than carried as a new-file hunk so
this patch stays small and reviewable. The diff below only touches function.cc.
xenia_trace.h needs no build-system change: the cpu CMakeLists globs *.h, and the
header is header-only / included by function.cc which is already in the build.)

---
diff --git a/src/xenia/cpu/function.cc b/src/xenia/cpu/function.cc
index c2dcf52..7a64faa 100644
--- a/src/xenia/cpu/function.cc
+++ b/src/xenia/cpu/function.cc
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include "xenia/base/logging.h"
 #include "xenia/cpu/symbol.h"
 #include "xenia/cpu/thread_state.h"
+#include "xenia/cpu/xenia_trace.h"  // L9-A golden-oracle guest-function trace

 namespace xe {
 namespace cpu {
@@ -132,6 +133,20 @@ uint32_t GuestFunction::MapMachineCodeToGuestAddress(
 bool GuestFunction::Call(ThreadState* thread_state, uint32_t return_address) {
   // SCOPE_profile_cpu_f("cpu");

+  // L9-A: emit a golden-oracle trace record on each guest-function entry.
+  // No-op unless XENIA_GUEST_TRACE=1 is set in the environment. We sample the
+  // guest entry PC (this->address()) plus the key PPC registers BEFORE the call
+  // runs so the L9-C bisector sees the entry state, matching how our recomp
+  // build's call tracer samples entries.
+  if (xe::trace::GuestTracer::Get().enabled()) {
+    auto* ctx = thread_state->context();
+    xe::trace::GuestTracer::Get().EmitFuncEntry(
+        address(),                       // guest_pc (function entry)
+        static_cast<uint32_t>(ctx->lr),  // caller return address
+        ctx->r[3], ctx->r[1],            // r3 (arg0), r1 (stack ptr)
+        thread_state->thread_id());      // interleaving context
+  }
+
   ThreadState* original_thread_state = ThreadState::Get();
   if (original_thread_state != thread_state) {
     ThreadState::Bind(thread_state);
